WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.446 --> 00:00:04.183
huge.

00:00:04.183 --> 00:00:08.855
&gt;&gt; General Zwack, appreciate

00:00:08.988 --> 00:00:09.422
your perspective, sir.

00:00:09.555 --> 00:00:09.789
Thank you.

00:00:10.189 --> 00:00:10.590
&gt;&gt;&gt; Last month, we learned the

00:00:10.723 --> 00:00:11.390
federal reserve chairman Jerome

00:00:11.524 --> 00:00:14.193
Powell was tricked by a fake

00:00:14.327 --> 00:00:14.894
call from Russian pranksters.

00:00:15.027 --> 00:00:15.628
Powell discussed global politics

00:00:15.762 --> 00:00:17.263
and the economy with someone he

00:00:17.396 --> 00:00:18.364
thought was the Ukrainian

00:00:18.498 --> 00:00:19.098
president zelenskyy.

00:00:19.232 --> 00:00:20.199
Turns out they were Russian

00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:20.900
supporters of Putin who

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:24.504
previously pranked other

00:00:24.637 --> 00:00:27.173
influential officials.

00:00:27.306 --> 00:00:29.842
CNN's Matthew chance had a

00:00:30.209 --> 00:00:30.543
chance to speak with the

00:00:30.676 --> 00:00:31.277
pranksters and investigate the

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.211
motive behind their tricks.

00:00:32.211 --> 00:00:39.886
Take a look.

00:00:40.219 --> 00:00:40.787
&gt;&gt; They're notorious pro-kremlin

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:41.554
pranksters.

00:00:41.687 --> 00:00:42.722
The Ukraine war has given them a

00:00:42.855 --> 00:00:44.323
new focus and new victims to

00:00:44.457 --> 00:00:46.225
deceive.

00:00:46.225 --> 00:00:47.026
&gt;&gt; Look who's there, Mr.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.494
President.

00:00:48.628 --> 00:00:49.862
&gt;&gt; Like George W. Bush, who

00:00:50.229 --> 00:00:55.134
thought he was speaking with the

00:00:55.268 --> 00:00:55.835
Ukrainian president, who had

00:00:56.235 --> 00:00:58.237
supposedly called to discuss the

00:00:58.337 --> 00:01:00.239
western military alliance.

00:01:00.339 --> 00:01:02.241
&gt;&gt; You always wanted to take

00:01:02.241 --> 00:01:04.243
Ukraine into nato, not Russia,

00:01:04.243 --> 00:01:04.777
but Ukraine, always, as I

00:01:04.911 --> 00:01:06.546
remember.

00:01:06.679 --> 00:01:09.148
&gt;&gt; That's right.

00:01:09.282 --> 00:01:09.916
You see, I felt Ukraine needed

00:01:10.249 --> 00:01:12.251
to be in the eu and in nato.

00:01:12.351 --> 00:01:14.821
[ Speaking non-english ]

00:01:14.954 --> 00:01:16.989
&gt;&gt; Reporter: A Russian official

00:01:17.123 --> 00:01:18.925
later told the pranksters it

00:01:19.058 --> 00:01:25.198
revealed the truth about

00:01:25.331 --> 00:01:25.865
long-time U.S. Ambitions to

00:01:26.265 --> 00:01:26.566
distance Russia from Ukraine.

00:01:26.699 --> 00:01:27.266
&gt;&gt; I'm glad you're not prank

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.267
calling me now.

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:29.202
&gt;&gt; Reporter: In getting to the

00:01:29.335 --> 00:01:30.369
truth, what would otherwise be

00:01:30.503 --> 00:01:31.571
left unspoken is what the

00:01:31.704 --> 00:01:32.805
pranksters told me they are all

00:01:32.939 --> 00:01:34.740
about.

00:01:34.874 --> 00:01:35.741
[ Speaking non-english ]

00:01:35.875 --> 00:01:38.978
&gt;&gt; Translator: First, it's about

00:01:39.111 --> 00:01:40.279
what this person is really like,

00:01:40.279 --> 00:01:43.216
how a president of a country

00:01:43.349 --> 00:01:44.283
behaves in an informal

00:01:44.283 --> 00:01:44.684
conversation.

00:01:44.817 --> 00:01:45.518
We're interested in getting more

00:01:45.651 --> 00:01:48.287
honest answers than we would in

00:01:48.287 --> 00:01:48.821
an ordinary public interview.

00:01:48.955 --> 00:01:52.458
&gt;&gt; One of the criticisms that is

00:01:52.592 --> 00:01:54.293
leveled against you is that

00:01:54.293 --> 00:01:56.295
you're always, you know,

00:01:56.295 --> 00:01:56.863
sympathetic to the Kremlin point

00:01:56.996 --> 00:01:58.297
of view.

00:01:58.297 --> 00:01:58.831
Let me ask you directly, are you

00:01:58.965 --> 00:02:00.800
working at the behest of the

00:02:00.933 --> 00:02:03.069
Kremlin to expose foreign

00:02:03.202 --> 00:02:04.303
officials or opponents of the

00:02:04.403 --> 00:02:09.175
Russian authorities?

00:02:09.308 --> 00:02:11.277
&gt;&gt; Translator: In general, it's

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:11.911
wrong to say that we are

00:02:12.311 --> 00:02:12.478
pro-kremlin.

00:02:12.612 --> 00:02:13.446
We're more pro-Russian

00:02:13.579 --> 00:02:14.313
pranksters, since this is our

00:02:14.313 --> 00:02:14.881
country that we love and worry

00:02:15.014 --> 00:02:17.984
about.

00:02:18.317 --> 00:02:21.621
You say that we only call those

00:02:21.754 --> 00:02:22.555
who are against the Kremlin, but

00:02:22.688 --> 00:02:23.589
the issue is that Russia simply

00:02:23.723 --> 00:02:25.558
doesn't have many friends now.

00:02:25.691 --> 00:02:28.327
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Ukraine, on

00:02:28.327 --> 00:02:31.163
the other hand, has many,

00:02:31.297 --> 00:02:31.998
especially in Washington, and

00:02:32.331 --> 00:02:33.366
posing as volodymyr zelenskyy,

00:02:33.499 --> 00:02:35.835
the Ukrainian president, has

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:36.969
gotten the Russian pranksters

00:02:37.103 --> 00:02:37.803
results.

00:02:37.937 --> 00:02:38.537
&gt;&gt; Just say it's a great honor

00:02:38.671 --> 00:02:41.240
to speak to you.

00:02:41.374 --> 00:02:43.676
&gt;&gt; Reporter: With influential

00:02:43.809 --> 00:02:44.377
figures like the chair of the

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:45.011
U.S. Federal reserve, who

00:02:45.144 --> 00:02:46.345
thought it was the real

00:02:46.345 --> 00:02:47.013
president zelenskyy quizzing him

00:02:47.146 --> 00:02:48.347
on the global economy and

00:02:48.347 --> 00:02:51.150
suggesting the fed let Ukraine

00:02:51.284 --> 00:02:52.351
print its own U.S. Dollars to

00:02:52.385 --> 00:02:54.820
fund the war with Russia.

00:02:54.954 --> 00:02:56.522
&gt;&gt; If you could present me

00:02:56.656 --> 00:02:57.556
printing press, I would be

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:01.694
really happy.

00:03:01.827 --> 00:03:04.563
&gt;&gt; We have one of those, but we

00:03:04.697 --> 00:03:05.364
keep it in the basement.

00:03:05.498 --> 00:03:08.801
&gt;&gt; Oh, okay.

00:03:08.935 --> 00:03:10.403
&gt;&gt; Again, I know you're going to

00:03:10.536 --> 00:03:11.404
be dependent on a lot of help

00:03:11.537 --> 00:03:12.371
from the west and from the

00:03:12.371 --> 00:03:15.308
United States.

00:03:15.441 --> 00:03:16.475
♪♪

00:03:16.609 --> 00:03:17.977
&gt;&gt; Reporter: It's not just U.S.

00:03:18.377 --> 00:03:20.446
Officials being pranked.

00:03:20.579 --> 00:03:21.547
&gt;&gt; We would like to continue the

00:03:21.681 --> 00:03:23.282
nuclear program in order to

00:03:23.416 --> 00:03:24.450
protect ourselves from Russia.

00:03:24.583 --> 00:03:26.652
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Britain's defense

00:03:26.786 --> 00:03:27.853
minister was taken aback when

00:03:27.987 --> 00:03:29.956
who he thought was Ukraine's

00:03:30.389 --> 00:03:30.690
prime minister floated the idea

00:03:30.823 --> 00:03:33.926
of nuclear weapons.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:37.463
&gt;&gt; I think more than being

00:03:37.596 --> 00:03:38.397
neutral, Russia would really

00:03:38.397 --> 00:03:39.999
hate that.

00:03:40.399 --> 00:03:40.533
&gt;&gt; For sure.

00:03:40.533 --> 00:03:43.235
We know this.

00:03:43.369 --> 00:03:44.904
&gt;&gt; Reporter: The British

00:03:45.037 --> 00:03:45.638
government condemned the prank

00:03:45.771 --> 00:03:46.405
as straight from the Kremlin

00:03:46.472 --> 00:03:52.478
playbook.

00:03:52.611 --> 00:03:53.212
&gt;&gt; Why haven't you prank called

00:03:53.346 --> 00:03:55.781
prominent people in Russia, like

00:03:55.915 --> 00:03:56.515
Vladimir Putin, like the head of

00:03:56.649 --> 00:03:58.017
the chechen republic, like

00:03:58.417 --> 00:03:59.018
prigozhin, the head of Wagner?

00:03:59.151 --> 00:04:00.086
Why aren't you crank calling

00:04:00.419 --> 00:04:01.253
those people to expose the truth

00:04:01.387 --> 00:04:06.425
about them?

00:04:06.425 --> 00:04:10.629
&gt;&gt; Make a disaster in our

00:04:10.763 --> 00:04:16.435
country because such calls could

00:04:16.502 --> 00:04:17.636
make damage in our current

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:20.072
situation.

00:04:20.439 --> 00:04:21.941
&gt;&gt; But you're not worried about

00:04:22.074 --> 00:04:22.942
the danger and the risks of

00:04:23.075 --> 00:04:24.510
doing what you do in other

00:04:24.643 --> 00:04:31.984
societies?

00:04:32.118 --> 00:04:34.453
&gt;&gt; That could hurt our society,

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:35.988
of course.

00:04:36.122 --> 00:04:36.722
&gt;&gt; Reporter: But the truth is,

00:04:36.856 --> 00:04:37.456
really powerful Russians would

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:38.457
never tolerate being pranked in

00:04:38.457 --> 00:04:41.994
this way.

00:04:42.128 --> 00:04:42.928
They would simply be unable to

00:04:43.062 --> 00:04:44.563
get away with duping a Kremlin

00:04:44.697 --> 00:04:49.101
that's cracked down hard on

00:04:49.235 --> 00:04:49.935
dissent, whereas Russia's

00:04:50.069 --> 00:04:52.071
enemies in the west, especially

00:04:52.471 --> 00:04:53.005
in the U.S., are considered fair

00:04:53.139 --> 00:04:54.740
game.

00:04:54.874 --> 00:04:55.441
&gt;&gt; Okay.

00:04:55.574 --> 00:04:56.108
Yeah.

00:04:56.475 --> 00:04:56.909
Thank you.

00:04:57.043 --> 00:04:57.676
&gt;&gt; Thank you very much.

